div.p:
Here the prophet further encourages us to
trust in the Lord for ever, and to continue waiting on him;
for,

I. He complains of the shameful stupidity
of this people, and their bent to backslide from God, speaking as
if he knew not what course to take with them. For,

div.h4:
Lamentation Caused by a Great Drought;
Prayer for Mercy; Pleading with God. (b.
c. 606.)

Judgment and Mercy; Restoration of the Jews;
Deliverance from Babylon. (b.
c. 605.)

div.p:
The prophet, having found his sleep sweet,
made so by the revelations of divine grace, sets himself to sleep
again, in hopes of further discoveries, and is not disappointed;
for it is here further promised,

div.h4:
Jeremiah Attempts to Quit Jerusalem;
Jeremiah Imprisoned; Jeremiah Favoured by the King. (b.
c. 589.)

The Prophet Ordered to Eat the Roll;
Instructions Given to the Prophet; The Prophet's Instructions;
Ezekiel's Reluctance to Be a Reprover. (b.
c. 595.)

Daniel Deals Plainly with Belshazzar;
Interpreting of the Writing on the Wall. (b.
c. 538.)

Daniel's Solicitude to Know the Times;
Period of Prophecy; Daniel Comforted. (b.
c. 534.)

Grounds of God's Controversy with Israel;
The Sins of the Priests and People. (b.
c. 758.)

Evil More Communicable than Good;
Encouragement to Build the Temple. (b.
c. 520.)

div.p:
Let us now see what this commandment is
which is for the priests, which, they must know, was sent to them;
and let us put into method the particulars of the charge.
